/* Prism GUI — "AlphaKore" theme (stone canvas, ink, Geist / Geist Mono / Doto; red for brand marks only)
   theme.py mirrors the subset the custom-painted widgets need. Keep both in
   step: every hex, size and radius below has a named twin over there, and the
   painted widgets read theme.py directly, so drift shows as a visible seam.

   ── Colour ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Six surfaces, one value each. Seventeen greys used to ship here with no rule
   about which meant what — three hairlines two units apart, two page greys,
   two wells. Nobody could tell a deliberate step from a typo, so each job now
   has exactly one hex:

     page background  #ffffff   CANVAS      card surface  #ffffff   CARD
     inset well       rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.02)   WELL        hairline      rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06)   HAIRLINE
     divider          #d0d0d1   DIVIDER     border        rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.10)   BORDER

     rail     #09090b  (= accent ramp 900 — see below)
     ink      #09090b
     accent   #09090b  ramp 100 rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.04) · 200 rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08) · 500 #71717a
                            600 #27272a · 700 #18181b · 800 #09090b · 900 #09090b
     neutral  400 #b7b7ba · 500 #98989b · 600 #7a7a7d · 700 #5d5d60 · 800 #424244
     semantic ok #186b53/#eafaf3 · warn #755a14/#fff8e8 · err #8a2f2f/#fdeeee
              info = the accent's own steps  (semantics never rotate; info does)

   Every status ink above clears WCAG AA 4.5:1 on its own tint. Two did not
   before this pass and were changed: warn ink was #8a6d1f (4.63, no headroom)
   and ok ink #1a7a5e (4.88). Hue unchanged in both; only the value moved.

   ── Type ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Eight levels, seven pixel sizes, and nothing else. Twenty distinct sizes
   shipped before this pass, nine of them inside one 4px band. Half a pixel is
   not a decision anyone can see.

     24px  PAGE_TITLE  Condensed 600   #h1 #h2 #stat
     18px  SECTION     Condensed 600   #h3 #h4 #statSm
     15px  CARD_TITLE  Condensed 600   #h5 #h6, primary button, the composer
     14px  BODY        Barlow 400      the global default
     13px  SUPPORT     Barlow 400      #body #lead, control labels
     12px  META        Barlow 500      #meta #dim #faint, timestamps, counts
     11px  LABEL       Condensed 600   #kick #colHead, tags, table headers
     12px  MONO        mono 500        #mono — ids, keys, paths

   Six heading object names collapse onto three real sizes so no panel has to
   be edited for the scale to take effect. Headings get their weight from
   condensation, not from size — the old #h1 was 30px, which on a 900px window
   spent a sixth of the vertical budget on a greeting.

   QSS has no letter-spacing property; the tracked labels (kickers, brand,
   window title) set it on their QFont in widgets/controls.py.

   ── Shape ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Three radii, not thirteen:
     6px   R_CHIP     pills, chips, badges, step marks, menu items, indicators
     8px   R_CONTROL  buttons, inputs, rows, small cards — every one of them
    12px   R_CARD     cards, panels, modals, dialogs, tables, group boxes
   999px   R_PILL     the special case: a true capsule at any height
     4px   R_MICRO    NOT a scale step — half the width of a progress bar or a
                      scrollbar handle, i.e. the radius that makes it a capsule
   Adding a value outside this scale is what makes an app stop feeling like one
   system. Reach for the nearest step instead.

   ── Spacing ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   4 / 8 / 12 / 16 / 20 / 28 / 40, and nothing between them. Page padding 28,
   card padding 20, card gutter 16, row spacing inside a card 12.

   ── Elevation ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Borders first, shadow rarely. A hairline is the default separator; shadow is
   reserved for things that genuinely float — modals, dropdowns, a dragged row.
   QSS has no box-shadow anyway, so a card's surface is styled here and its
   shadow attached in Python by widgets.controls.elevate(), which is off by
   default. See controls.shadows_enabled() for why.

   ── Focus ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Every interactive control below carries a visible :focus ring, and every one
   of them keeps its box the same size while wearing it: the ring is 2px and
   the padding drops by 1px to pay for it. Without that compensation a focus
   ring reflows the row it is in, which reads as the layout twitching under the
   keyboard and is worse than no ring at all.

   ── Role colour ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Every accent hex here is rewritten at load time by theme.role_stylesheet()
   so the whole app takes the signed-in role's hue. That includes the rail,
   which is deliberately accent-ramp-900 rather than a separate navy — a role
   that moved everything else but left a blue rail would look broken.

   The swap is a blunt string replace over eleven fixed hexes
   (theme._ACCENT_HEXES). So: an accent-coloured hex written here that is NOT
   one of those eleven will not rotate, and will strand one permanently blue
   element in a green copy. And a hex that must NOT rotate — every neutral,
   every semantic, every tool brand colour — has to be distinct from all
   eleven. "Won" stays green in every role. */

* {
    font-family: "Geist", "Inter", system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", "Ubuntu", "DejaVu Sans", sans-serif;
    font-size: 15px;
    color: #111110;
}

QMainWindow, QWidget#central, QWidget#columns, QWidget#centralWidget {
    background: transparent;
}

QScrollArea, QScrollArea > QWidget, QScrollArea > QWidget > QWidget {
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
}

/* ── Modals & Dialogs: Solid surfaces to eliminate Linux X11 pitch-black window bugs ── */
QDialog {
    background-color: #ffffff;
    color: #111110;
}

QDialog #dialogHeader {
    background-color: #ffffff;
    border: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #E6E5E1;
}

QDialog #dialogFooter {
    background-color: #fbfbfb;
    border: none;
    border-top: 1px solid #E6E5E1;
}

QDialog #dialogFooter QPushButton {
    min-height: 28px;
    padding: 5px 16px;
}

QDialog #dialogFooter #primaryBtn, QDialog #dialogFooter #primary {
    min-height: 28px;
    padding: 5px 20px;
}

QDialog #dialogBody, QDialog QWidget#dialogBody {
    background-color: #ffffff;
}

QDialog QScrollArea,
QDialog QScrollArea > QWidget,
QDialog QScrollArea > QWidget > QWidget {
    background-color: #ffffff;
    background: #ffffff;
    border: none;
}

QDialog QListWidget {
    background-color: #ffffff;
    color: #111110;
    border: 1px solid #D8D7D2;
    border-radius: 8px;
}

QDialog QTextBrowser,
QDialog QPlainTextEdit,
QDialog QTextEdit,
QDialog QLineEdit {
    background-color: #ffffff;
    color: #111110;
    border: 1px solid #D8D7D2;
    border-radius: 8px;
}

QDialog QComboBox {
    background-color: #ffffff;
    color: #111110;
    border: 1px solid #D8D7D2;
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 4px 8px;
}

QDialog QLabel {
    color: #111110;
}

/* Qt hands QDialogButtonBox platform icons */
QDialogButtonBox {
    dialogbuttonbox-buttons-have-icons: 0;
}

QToolTip {
    background: #111110;
    color: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid #2a2a28;
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 5px 8px;
    font-size: 13px;
}

/* ── the card: transparent shell — Card.paintEvent paints all glass layers ── */
#card {
    background: transparent;
    border-radius: 18px;
    border: none;
}

#card QLabel {
    color: #111110;
}

/* An inset well inside a card */
#well, #card #well {
    background: #F6F5F2;
    border: 1px solid #E6E5E1;
    border-radius: 12px;
}

/* Hairline between rows inside a card. */
#cardLine {
    background: #EFEEEA;
    max-height: 1px;
    min-height: 1px;
    border: none;
}

/* The vertical separator between the work column and the context rail. */
#railLine {
    background: #EFEEEA;
    max-width: 1px;
    min-width: 1px;
    border: none;
}

/* ── sidebar: floating rounded pure glassmorphic nav rail ───────── */
#sidebar {
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 20px;
}

#sidebarInner {
    background: transparent;
}

#addonsHead, #helpHead, #settingsHead {
    background: transparent;
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 2px 4px;
}

#addonsHead:hover, #helpHead:hover, #settingsHead:hover {
    background: #F6F5F2;
}

#addonsChevron, #helpChevron, #settingsChevron {
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 0;
}

#addonsChevron:hover, #helpChevron:hover, #settingsChevron:hover {
    background: #EFEEEA;
}

#railCollapseBtn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px solid transparent;
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 0;
}

#railCollapseBtn:hover {
    background: #F6F5F2;
    border-color: #E6E5E1;
}

#railCollapseBtn:pressed {
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.09);
}

#sidebar[collapsed="true"] #navItem,
#sidebar[collapsed="true"] #navSub,
#sidebar[collapsed="true"] #railPrimary {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 4px 0px;
}

#sidebar[collapsed="true"] #navItem[cur="true"],
#sidebar[collapsed="true"] #navSub[cur="true"] {
    background: #EFEEEA;
    border: 1px solid #D8D7D2;
    border-radius: 8px;
}

#sidebar[collapsed="true"] #railProfile {
    border-top: none;
    padding: 0;
}

#brand {
    font-family: "Geist";
    font-size: 21px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #111110;
}

#navItem {
    text-align: left;
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px solid transparent;
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 8px 12px;
    font-family: "Geist";
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #2a2a28;
}

#navItem:hover {
    background: #F6F5F2;
    color: #111110;
}

#navItem:pressed {
    background: #EFEEEA;
}

#navItem:focus, #navSub:focus, #railProfile:focus {
    border-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
}

#navItem[cur="true"] {
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid #D8D7D2;
    color: #111110;
    font-weight: 700;
}

#navSub {
    text-align: left;
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px solid transparent;
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 7px 12px;
    font-family: "Geist";
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #2a2a28;
}

#navSub:hover {
    background: #F6F5F2;
    color: #111110;
}

#navSub[cur="true"] {
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid #D8D7D2;
    color: #111110;
    font-weight: 700;
}

#navItem[locked="true"], #navSub[locked="true"] {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.40);
}

#navItem[locked="true"]:hover, #navSub[locked="true"]:hover {
    background: #F6F5F2;
    color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65);
}

#navSub:disabled {
    color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25);
}

#navSection {
    font-family: "Geist";
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.50);
    padding: 3px 4px;
    background: transparent;
    letter-spacing: 0.6px;
}

#railRule {
    background: #EFEEEA;
    max-height: 1px;
    min-height: 1px;
    border: none;
}

#railMuted {
    font-size: 13.5px;
    color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.45);
    background: transparent;
}

/* The New-task button */
#railPrimary {
    background: #111110;
    border: 1px solid #111110;
    border-radius: 8px;
    color: #ffffff;
    font-family: "Geist";
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 17px;
    padding: 9px 12px;
    text-align: center;
}

#railPrimary:hover { background: #2a2a28; border-color: #2a2a28; }
#railPrimary:pressed { background: #000000; }
#railPrimary:focus { border-color: #111110; }
#railPrimary:disabled {
    background: #F6F5F2;
    border-color: #D8D7D2;
    color: #a1a1aa;
}

/* The profile row */
#railProfile {
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px solid transparent;
    border-top: 1px solid #E6E5E1;
    border-radius: 0;
    text-align: left;
    padding: 8px 6px;
}

#railProfile:hover { background: #F6F5F2; }

#railProfileName {
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #111110;
    background: transparent;
}

#railProfileRole {
    font-size: 13.5px;
    color: #6b6a65;
    background: transparent;
}

#hr {
    background: #EFEEEA;
    max-height: 1px;
    min-height: 1px;
    border: none;
}

/* ── type roles ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Eight levels. Every object name that existed before still resolves, so no
   panel has to change for the scale to land — the six heading levels simply
   collapse onto the three sizes that are actually distinguishable. */

/* LABEL — the uppercase tracked micro-label. Tracking is set on the QFont by
   controls.kicker(); QSS cannot express it. */
#kick, #colHead {
    font-family: "Geist Mono";
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #6b6a65;
}

#kickMuted {
    font-family: "Geist Mono";
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #6b6a65;
}

/* PAGE_TITLE — one per screen. */
#h1, #h2 { font-family: "Geist"; font-size: 26px; font-weight: 600; color: #111110; }
#card #h1, #card #h2 { color: #111110; }
/* SECTION — the heading above a group of cards. */
#h3, #h4 { font-family: "Geist"; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; color: #111110; }
#card #h3, #card #h4 { color: #111110; }
/* CARD_TITLE — the name of a thing. */
#h5, #h6 { font-family: "Geist"; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600; color: #111110; }
#card #h5, #card #h6 { color: #111110; }

/* The dashboard's big condensed figure — "12", "₹8.4L", "58%". A metric is a
   page title in a card, so it takes the same two steps. */
#stat {
    font-family: "Geist";
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 26px;
    color: #111110;
}

#statSm {
    font-family: "Geist";
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 20px;
    color: #111110;
}

#card #stat, #card #statSm {
    color: #111110;
}

/* META — timestamps, durations, counts. */
#meta, #dim {
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #2a2a28;
}

/* The secondary metadata step — guaranteed high contrast on any wallpaper. */
#faint {
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #6b6a65;
}

/* SUPPORT — sentences under a title, and the standard control label. */
#body, #lead, #support {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: #2a2a28;
}

/* MONO — ids, keys, device codes, paths. No mono face is vendored; see
   theme.FONT_MONO_STACK for why. */
#mono {
    font-family: "Geist Mono", "JetBrains Mono", "DejaVu Sans Mono", "Menlo", "Consolas", monospace;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #2a2a28;
}

/* dashed advisory box (the "Tip." card in the context rail) */
#note {
    border: 1px dashed rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.10);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 12px;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #6b6a65;
}

/* The bare-label empty state. Kept because nine call sites set it, but the
   real one is controls.EmptyState — this is the text-only degenerate case.
   Its ink was #98989b, which is 2.6:1 on the canvas: the one message on an
   otherwise empty screen, and the hardest thing on it to read. */
#emptyState {
    color: #6b6a65;
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 20px 16px;
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px dashed rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.10);
    border-radius: 12px;
}

/* The title and body inside controls.EmptyState, which draws its own icon pad
   and button rather than being one dashed label. */
#emptyTitle {
    font-family: "Geist";
    font-size: 18px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #111110;
    background: transparent;
}

#emptyBody {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: #6b6a65;
    background: transparent;
}

/* ── buttons ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Exactly four variants. Eleven named button object names shipped before this
   pass and they were not four ideas with eleven names — they were eleven
   half-specified boxes, several missing hover, most missing focus, one
   (`#primary`) missing a rule entirely so three "run" CTAs rendered as plain
   hairline boxes. Every one of those names still works; each now resolves to
   one of the four below, plus a size or shape modifier.

     PRIMARY      solid accent      #primaryBtn #primary #railPrimary
                  one per surface
     SECONDARY    outlined neutral  the bare QPushButton default, #smallBtn,
                  the workhorse     #iconBtn #micBtn #chipBtn #secondaryBtn
     TERTIARY     text / ghost      #ghostBtn #linkBtn #tabBtn #secBtn
                  in-place actions  #tertiaryBtn
     DESTRUCTIVE  outlined red      #dangerBtn #destructiveBtn
                  irreversible only

   All four carry :hover, :pressed, :focus and :disabled. */

/* SECONDARY — tactile frosted pill with high-contrast ink label. */
QPushButton, #secondaryBtn {
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid #D8D7D2;
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 5px 16px;
    min-height: 28px;
    font-family: "Geist";
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #111110;
}

QPushButton:hover, #secondaryBtn:hover {
    background: #ffffff;
    border-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25);
    color: #000000;
}

QPushButton:pressed, #secondaryBtn:pressed {
    background: rgba(240, 240, 240, 0.95);
    border-color: #111110;
    color: #000000;
}

QPushButton:focus, #secondaryBtn:focus {
    border-color: #111110;
    color: #111110;
}

QPushButton:disabled, #secondaryBtn:disabled {
    color: rgba(9, 9, 11, 0.40);
    border-color: #E6E5E1;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.45);
}

/* PRIMARY — solid accent, one per surface. Flat: the fill is a single colour,
   not a gradient. A vertical gradient on a filled button is the single most
   dating thing an interface can wear, and it also breaks the role swap, which
   rewrites flat hexes and cannot see into a qlineargradient's stops. */
#primaryBtn, #primary {
    background: #111110;
    border: 1px solid #111110;
    border-radius: 8px;
    color: #ffffff;
    padding: 6px 20px;
    min-height: 34px;
    font-family: "Geist";
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
}

#primaryBtn:hover, #primary:hover {
    background: #2a2a28;
    border-color: #2a2a28;
}

#primaryBtn:pressed, #primary:pressed {
    background: #2a2a28;
    border-color: #2a2a28;
}

/* The ring on a filled button has to be darker than the fill, not lighter —
   a white ring on accent disappears against the card behind it. */
#primaryBtn:focus, #primary:focus {
    border-color: #111110;
}

/* Not greyed to a flat neutral: the button keeps its identity and simply
   loses weight, so it still reads as the thing to press once there is
   something to press it for. Both hexes are ramp steps, so a disabled primary
   rotates with the role like the live one — it used to be a hardcoded
   #c7d3dc, which stayed blue in a green copy. */
#primaryBtn:disabled, #primary:disabled {
    background: #EFEEEA;
    border-color: #E6E5E1;
    color: #2a2a28;
}

/* TERTIARY — no box until you touch it. For in-place actions that must not
   compete with the surface's one primary. */
#ghostBtn, #tertiaryBtn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid transparent;
    border-radius: 8px;
    color: #2a2a28;
    padding: 5px 8px;
    min-height: 18px;
    font-family: "Geist";
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
}

#ghostBtn:hover, #tertiaryBtn:hover {
    background: #F6F5F2;
    color: #111110;
}

#ghostBtn:pressed, #tertiaryBtn:pressed {
    background: #EFEEEA;
}

#ghostBtn:focus, #tertiaryBtn:focus {
    border-color: #111110;
}

#ghostBtn:disabled, #tertiaryBtn:disabled {
    color: #b7b7ba;
    background: transparent;
}

/* TERTIARY, inline-link shape: left-aligned, tighter, for a run of them in a
   column. Same colour model as #ghostBtn. */
#linkBtn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid transparent;
    border-radius: 6px;
    color: #2a2a28;
    font-family: "Geist";
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 500;
    padding: 4px 6px;
    min-height: 18px;
    text-align: left;
}

#linkBtn:hover {
    color: #111110;
    background: #F6F5F2;
}

#linkBtn:pressed { background: #EFEEEA; }
#linkBtn:focus { border-color: #111110; }
#linkBtn:disabled { color: #b7b7ba; background: transparent; }

/* DESTRUCTIVE — outlined red, filled only once pressed. Deliberately not a
   solid red button at rest: an irreversible action should be reachable, not
   the loudest thing on the screen. */
#dangerBtn, #destructiveBtn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid #eecccc;
    border-radius: 8px;
    color: #a3141a;
    padding: 6px 13px;
    min-height: 18px;
    font-family: "Geist";
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
}

#dangerBtn:hover, #destructiveBtn:hover {
    background: #f7e3e1;
    border-color: #a3141a;
}

#dangerBtn:pressed, #destructiveBtn:pressed {
    background: #a3141a;
    border-color: #a3141a;
    color: #ffffff;
}

#dangerBtn:focus, #destructiveBtn:focus {
    border-color: #a3141a;
    background: #f7e3e1;
}

#dangerBtn:disabled, #destructiveBtn:disabled {
    color: #b7b7ba;
    border-color: #E6E5E1;
    background: transparent;
}

/* ── button modifiers ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Size and shape only. Each of these inherits its colour model from one of
   the four variants above, which is why none of them repeats a hover or a
   focus rule. */

/* SECONDARY at the small step. */
#smallBtn {
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 5px 11px;
    border-radius: 6px;
}


/* SECONDARY, square, glyph only. 34px keeps it past the 28px minimum target
   with room for the ring. */
#iconBtn {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.25);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 0;
    min-width: 34px;
    max-width: 34px;
    min-height: 34px;
    max-height: 34px;
}

#iconBtn:hover {
    background: #F6F5F2;
}

/* .mic-lg — the composer's mic. Neutral until armed, then it goes red,
   because "recording" is a state you must be able to see from across a
   workshop and an accent-blue mic looks identical to every other control. */
#micBtn {
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid #D8D7D2;
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 5px 16px;
    min-height: 28px;
    font-family: "Geist";
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #111110;
}

#micBtn:hover {
    background: #ffffff;
    border-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25);
    color: #000000;
}

#micBtn:pressed {
    background: rgba(240, 240, 240, 0.95);
    border-color: #111110;
    color: #000000;
}

#micBtn:focus {
    border-color: #111110;
    color: #111110;
}

#micBtn:checked {
    background: #f7e3e1;
    border-color: #eecccc;
    color: #a3141a;
}

#micBtn:checked:focus {
    border-color: #a3141a;
}

/* SECONDARY in capsule form — the quick-start chips on the hero card, and the
   filter chips on History and AI tools. */
#chipBtn {
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid #D8D7D2;
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 5px 13px;
    min-height: 18px;
    font-family: "Geist";
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #111110;
}

#chipBtn:hover {
    background: #ffffff;
    border-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.20);
    color: #111110;
}

#chipBtn:pressed {
    background: #EFEEEA;
}

#chipBtn:focus {
    border-color: #111110;
    color: #111110;
}

/* A filter chip that is on. Filled tint rather than an outline, so a row of
   eight chips shows its one selection from across the screen. */
#chipBtn:checked, #chipBtn[cur="true"] {
    background: #111110;
    border-color: #111110;
    color: #ffffff;
}

#chipBtn:disabled {
    color: #b7b7ba;
    border-color: #E6E5E1;
}

/* The segmented tab strip on Inquiry Automation, and controls.Tabs. */
#tabStrip {
    background: #F6F5F2;
    border: 1px solid #E6E5E1;
    border-radius: 12px;
}

/* TERTIARY, segmented. */
#tabBtn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid transparent;
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 6px 15px;
    min-height: 18px;
    font-family: "Geist";
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #6b6a65;
}

#tabBtn:hover { background: #F6F5F2; }
#tabBtn:pressed { background: #E6E5E1; }
#tabBtn:focus { border-color: #111110; }
#tabBtn:disabled { color: #b7b7ba; }

#tabBtn[cur="true"], #tabBtn:checked {
    background: #F6F5F2;
    color: #111110;
}

/* TERTIARY, full-width and left-aligned — the Settings section list. */
#secBtn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px solid transparent;
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 7px 12px;
    min-height: 20px;
    font-family: "Geist";
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #2a2a28;
    text-align: left;
}

#secBtn:hover {
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.035);
    color: #111110;
}
#secBtn:pressed {
    background: #EFEEEA;
}
#secBtn:focus {
    border-color: #D8D7D2;
}
#secBtn:disabled {
    color: #a1a1aa;
}

#secBtn[cur="true"] {
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.065);
    border: 1px solid #E6E5E1;
    color: #111110;
    font-weight: 600;
}

/* ── inputs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   2px border at rest in the border grey, so the accent focus ring can replace
   the colour without changing the box. */
QTextEdit, QLineEdit, QComboBox, QListWidget, QPlainTextEdit {
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid #D8D7D2;
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 6px 11px;
    color: #111110;
    selection-background-color: #111110;
    selection-color: #ffffff;
}

QTextEdit:hover, QLineEdit:hover, QComboBox:hover {
    border-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.22);
}

QTextEdit:focus, QLineEdit:focus, QComboBox:focus, QPlainTextEdit:focus {
    border-color: #111110;
}

QTextEdit:disabled, QLineEdit:disabled, QComboBox:disabled,
QPlainTextEdit:disabled {
    background: #F6F5F2;
    border-color: #E6E5E1;
    color: #a1a1aa;
}

/* Lists don't take the accent focus ring on the box: a selected row already
   says where you are, and ringing the whole list reads as an error state. */
QListWidget:focus {
    border-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
}

/* The task card's own editor sits *inside* the composer card, so it drops the
   second border and reads as bare text on the card. It is the one input on the
   screen and takes the CARD_TITLE step at body weight, so it feels like the
   subject of the page rather than another field.

   Its focus cue is an underline rather than a ring, because a ring around a
   borderless editor inside a bordered card is three boxes deep. The
   transparent border reserves the space, so nothing moves when it lights. */
#taskEdit {
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
    border-bottom: 2px solid transparent;
    border-radius: 0;
    padding: 0;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: #111110;
}

#taskEdit:focus {
    border-bottom-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.40);
}

/* controls.SearchField — a QLineEdit with a leading glyph and a clear action.
   Capsule rather than rounded-rect: a search box is the one input that reads
   faster as a pill, and it is always the first thing in a toolbar. */
#searchField {
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 6px 14px;
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid #D8D7D2;
    color: #111110;
}

/* The clear button Qt inserts for setClearButtonEnabled(), and the leading
   search glyph, are both QToolButtons Qt sizes at 22x18 — under the 28px
   minimum target, and the last thing left in the app's click-target audit
   (it showed up on AI tools, History and Help at once). Qt will not let a
   fixed width/height through here, but it honours the minimums, which lands
   them on exactly 28x28 inside a 36px field. */
#searchField QToolButton {
    min-width: 28px;
    min-height: 28px;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    border: 0;
}

QComboBox {
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1.5px solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.22);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 6px 32px 6px 12px;
    min-height: 20px;
    color: #111110;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
}

QComboBox:hover {
    background: #ffffff;
    border-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.40);
}

QComboBox:focus {
    border-color: #111110;
}

QComboBox::drop-down {
    subcontrol-origin: padding;
    subcontrol-position: top right;
    width: 28px;
    border: none;
    background: transparent;
}

QComboBox::down-arrow {
    image: url(%ASSETS%/caret-down.svg);
    width: 14px;
    height: 14px;
    margin-right: 8px;
}

QComboBox QAbstractItemView {
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1.5px solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.20);
    border-radius: 8px;
    selection-background-color: #111110;
    selection-color: #ffffff;
    padding: 4px;
    color: #111110;
    outline: none;
}

QComboBox QAbstractItemView::item {
    min-height: 26px;
    padding: 5px 10px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    color: #111110;
}

QComboBox QAbstractItemView::item:selected {
    background: #111110;
    color: #ffffff;
}

QComboBox QAbstractItemView::item:hover {
    background: #EFEEEA;
    color: #111110;
}

QListWidget {
    padding: 3px;
}

QListWidget::item {
    padding: 7px 9px;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 6px;
}

QListWidget::item:hover {
    background: #F6F5F2;
}

QListWidget::item:selected {
    background: #F6F5F2;
    color: #111110;
}

/* ── rows ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   A plan step / mention / stage. On the canvas these are their own small
   cards; inside a card they are transparent rows split by #cardLine. Rows take
   R_CONTROL and the card around them R_CARD, so the card stays deliberately
   looser than its own contents. */
#row {
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid #E6E5E1;
    border-radius: 10px;
    color: #111110;
}

#row:hover {
    background: #ffffff;
    border-color: #D8D7D2;
}

#row QLabel {
    color: #111110;
}

#rowFlat {
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 8px;
}

#rowFlat:hover {
    background: #F6F5F2;
}

#rowFlat QLabel {
    color: #111110;
}

#rowMuted {
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px solid #E6E5E1;
    border-radius: 8px;
}

/* controls.FileItem and controls.StepRow — a row that is its own hairline box
   on the canvas rather than a band inside a card. */
#listRow {
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid #E6E5E1;
    border-radius: 10px;
    color: #111110;
}

#listRow:hover {
    background: #ffffff;
    border-color: #D8D7D2;
}

#listRow QLabel {
    color: #111110;
}

/* the step marker painted by controls.StepMark */
#stepMark {
    background: #E6E5E1;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 6px;
}

#stepMark[on="true"] {
    background: #111110;
}

/* The 1 Describe → 2 Plan → 3 Run breadcrumb. */
#stepCur {
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #111110;
}

#stepOff {
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #6b6a65;
}

/* ── headers and toolbars ────────────────────────────────────────────────
   The two standard bands: PageHeader is fixed at the top of a screen and never
   scrolls; SectionHeader sits above a group of cards inside the scroll. Both
   are drawn by widgets/controls.py so every screen gets the same one. */
#pageHeader {
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
}

#pageTitle {
    font-family: "Geist";
    font-size: 26px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #111110;
    background: transparent;
}

#pageSubtitle {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: #2a2a28;
    background: transparent;
}

#pageHeader QPushButton {
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid #D8D7D2;
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 6px 14px;
    min-height: 20px;
    font-family: "Geist";
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #111110;
}

#pageHeader QPushButton:hover {
    background: #ffffff;
    border-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25);
}

#sectionHeader {
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
}

#sectionTitle {
    font-family: "Geist";
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #111110;
    background: transparent;
}

#sectionSubtitle {
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #2a2a28;
    background: transparent;
}

#card #sectionTitle, #card #h1, #card #h2, #card #h3, #card #h4, #card #h5, #card #h6, #card #stat, #card #statSm {
    color: #111110;
}

#card #sectionSubtitle {
    color: #6b6a65;
}

/* ── licence & update banner ─────────────────────────────────────────── */
#licenceBanner {
    background: rgba(18, 20, 26, 0.85);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
}

#licenceBanner QLabel {
    color: #f1f5f9;
}

#licenceBanner QPushButton {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.15);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.25);
    color: #ffffff;
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 4px 10px;
}

#licenceBanner QPushButton:hover {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.25);
    border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.45);
}

/* A sticky strip of search / filter / actions above a long list. */
#toolbar {
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid #E6E5E1;
    border-radius: 12px;
}

/* ── tags ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Pills. controls.Pill sets its own colours inline for the tones that vary by
   data; these object names remain for the fixed ones, and both now read the
   same pairs — theme.TAG_TONES. They used to disagree: controls.Chip carried
   a second Python colour dict and rendered a "warning" chip grey-on-amber and
   a "success" chip blue-on-green while a plain QLabel wearing the same object
   name got the right ink from here. */
#tagAccent, #tagOutline, #tagNeutral, #tagWarn, #tagErr, #tagOk {
    font-size: 12px;
    padding: 3px 11px;
    border-radius: 999px;
}

#tagAccent { background: #F6F5F2; color: #111110; border: 1px solid #E6E5E1; }
#tagOutline { background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.35); color: #ffffff; }
#tagNeutral { background: #E6E5E1; color: #2a2a28; border: 1px solid #D8D7D2; }
#tagOk { background: #e4efe7; color: #1f6b43; border: 1px solid #e4efe7; }
#tagWarn { background: #fff8e8; color: #755a14; border: 1px solid #fff8e8; }
#tagErr { background: #f7e3e1; color: #a3141a; border: 1px solid #f7e3e1; }

/* ── output stage body ───────────────────────────────────────────────── */
#stageBody {
    background: #F6F5F2;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 12px;
    font-size: 14px;
    color: #6b6a65;
}

/* ── checkbox ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
QCheckBox, QRadioButton {
    color: #111110;
    spacing: 8px;
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
    outline: none;
}

QCheckBox:focus, QRadioButton:focus {
    border: none;
    background: transparent;
    outline: none;
}

QCheckBox::indicator {
    width: 16px;
    height: 16px;
    border: 1.5px solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
    border-radius: 4px;
    background: #ffffff;
}

QCheckBox::indicator:hover {
    border-color: #111110;
}

/* The indicator is the only visible part of a checkbox, so the focus cue has
   to land on it — a ring around the label text would say nothing.
   Subcontrol (::indicator) must precede pseudo-state (:focus). */
QCheckBox::indicator:focus, QRadioButton::indicator:focus {
    border: 2px solid #111110;
}

QCheckBox::indicator:checked {
    background: #111110;
    border: 1.5px solid #111110;
    /* %ASSETS% is rewritten to an absolute path by main.py — a bare relative
       url() would resolve against the process's cwd, not the app. */
    image: url(%ASSETS%/check.svg);
}

QCheckBox:disabled {
    color: #b7b7ba;
}

QCheckBox::indicator:disabled {
    background: #F6F5F2;
    border-color: #E6E5E1;
}

/* ── tabs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Neither this stylesheet nor the one before it ever styled QTabWidget, so
   the tab pane fell through to the desktop palette. On a machine running a
   dark GTK/KDE theme that painted the whole body of the setup dialogs
   near-black behind our dark ink — unreadable, and nothing to do with the
   app's own theme. Everything Qt can paint has to be named here.

   Shaped like the segmented strip on Inquiry Automation, so a tab reads the
   same whether it is in a dialog or on a screen. */
QTabWidget::pane {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.15);
    border-radius: 12px;
    top: -1px;
}

QTabWidget > QWidget {
    background: transparent;
}

QTabBar {
    background: transparent;
    qproperty-drawBase: 0;
}

QTabBar::tab {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid transparent;
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 6px 15px;
    margin: 0 4px 4px 0;
    font-family: "Geist";
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #6b6a65;
}

QTabBar::tab:hover {
    background: #F6F5F2;
}

QTabBar::tab:selected {
    background: #F6F5F2;
    color: #111110;
}

QTabBar::tab:focus {
    border-color: #111110;
}

QTabBar::tab:disabled {
    color: #b7b7ba;
}

/* ── tables ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
QTableWidget, QTableView {
    background: #ffffff;
    alternate-background-color: #f9f9fb;
    border: 1px solid #D8D7D2;
    border-radius: 8px;
    gridline-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);
    selection-background-color: #EFEEEA;
    selection-color: #111110;
    color: #111110;
    outline: none;
}

QTableWidget::item, QTableView::item {
    padding: 7px 10px;
    border: none;
    color: #111110;
    outline: none;
}

QTableWidget::item:selected, QTableView::item:selected {
    background: #EFEEEA;
    color: #111110;
    outline: none;
}

QTableWidget::item:focus, QTableView::item:focus {
    background: #EFEEEA;
    color: #111110;
    outline: none;
    border: none;
}

QHeaderView {
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
    outline: none;
}

QHeaderView::section {
    background: #f6f5f2;
    border: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #D8D7D2;
    padding: 8px 10px;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #6b6a65;
}

QTableCornerButton::section {
    background: #f6f5f2;
    border: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #D8D7D2;
}

/* ── Email compose: CSV recipients table ─────────────────────────────── */
QTableWidget#emailRecipientsTable {
    background: #ffffff;
    alternate-background-color: #fafafa;
    border: 1px solid #D8D7D2;
    border-radius: 8px;
    gridline-color: transparent;
    selection-background-color: #EFEEEA;
    selection-color: #111110;
    color: #111110;
    outline: none;
}

QTableWidget#emailRecipientsTable::item {
    padding: 7px 12px;
    border: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #E6E5E1;
    color: #111110;
    font-size: 13px;
    outline: none;
}

QTableWidget#emailRecipientsTable::item:selected {
    background: #EFEEEA;
    color: #111110;
    outline: none;
}

QTableWidget#emailRecipientsTable::item:focus {
    outline: none;
    border: none;
}

QTableWidget#emailRecipientsTable QHeaderView::section {
    background: #f6f5f2;
    border: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #D8D7D2;
    padding: 8px 12px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #6b6a65;
}

/* ── the rest of what Qt can paint ───────────────────────────────────── */
QTextBrowser {
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid #D8D7D2;
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 10px 12px;
    color: #111110;
}

/* ── Toast notifications ────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
QFrame#toastNotification {
    background: #111110;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.16);
    border-radius: 12px;
}

QRadioButton {
    color: #111110;
    spacing: 8px;
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
    outline: none;
}

QRadioButton:focus {
    border: none;
    background: transparent;
    outline: none;
}

QRadioButton::indicator {
    width: 16px;
    height: 16px;
    border: 1.5px solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.30);
    border-radius: 9px;
    background: #ffffff;
}

QRadioButton::indicator:hover {
    border-color: #111110;
}

QRadioButton::indicator:checked {
    border: 1.5px solid #111110;
    background: qradialgradient(cx: 0.5, cy: 0.5, radius: 0.5, fx: 0.5, fy: 0.5,
                                stop: 0 #111110, stop: 0.45 #111110,
                                stop: 0.50 transparent, stop: 1 transparent);
}

QRadioButton:disabled { color: #a1a1aa; }

QSpinBox, QDoubleSpinBox, QTimeEdit, QDateEdit, QDateTimeEdit {
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid #D8D7D2;
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 5px 9px;
    color: #111110;
    selection-background-color: #111110;
    selection-color: #ffffff;
}

QSpinBox:hover, QDoubleSpinBox:hover, QTimeEdit:hover, QDateEdit:hover, QDateTimeEdit:hover {
    border-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.18);
}

QSpinBox:focus, QDoubleSpinBox:focus, QTimeEdit:focus, QDateEdit:focus, QDateTimeEdit:focus {
    border-color: #111110;
}

QSpinBox:disabled, QDoubleSpinBox:disabled, QTimeEdit:disabled, QDateTimeEdit:disabled,
QDateEdit:disabled {
    background: #F6F5F2;
    border-color: #E6E5E1;
    color: #b7b7ba;
}

/* The steppers. Left unstyled they fall through to the desktop's own arrows,
   which on this system drew as a bare angular bracket half outside the box —
   the same gap that made the tab pane render dark. Sized generously on
   purpose: these are pressed by somebody setting a GST rate, not a developer
   nudging a value. */
QSpinBox::up-button, QDoubleSpinBox::up-button,
QTimeEdit::up-button, QDateEdit::up-button, QDateTimeEdit::up-button {
    subcontrol-origin: border;
    subcontrol-position: top right;
    width: 24px;
    height: 17px;
    border: none;
    border-top-right-radius: 8px;
    background: transparent;
    image: url(%ASSETS%/caret-up.svg);
}

QSpinBox::down-button, QDoubleSpinBox::down-button,
QTimeEdit::down-button, QDateEdit::down-button, QDateTimeEdit::down-button {
    subcontrol-origin: border;
    subcontrol-position: bottom right;
    width: 24px;
    height: 17px;
    border: none;
    border-bottom-right-radius: 8px;
    background: transparent;
    image: url(%ASSETS%/caret-down.svg);
}

QSpinBox::up-button:hover, QSpinBox::down-button:hover,
QDoubleSpinBox::up-button:hover, QDoubleSpinBox::down-button:hover {
    background: #E6E5E1;
}

QSpinBox::up-arrow, QSpinBox::down-arrow,
QDoubleSpinBox::up-arrow, QDoubleSpinBox::down-arrow {
    width: 12px;
    height: 12px;
}

QProgressBar {
    background: #E6E5E1;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 9px;
    height: 18px;
    min-height: 18px;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #ffffff;
}

QProgressBar::chunk {
    background: qlineargradient(x1:0, y1:0, x2:1, y2:0,
                                stop:0 #6c63ff, stop:1 #a78bfa);
    border-radius: 9px;
    width: 30px;
    margin: 1px;
}

QToolButton {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid transparent;
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 4px;
    color: #2a2a28;
}

QToolButton:hover { background: #F6F5F2; }
QToolButton:pressed { background: #E6E5E1; }
QToolButton:focus { border-color: #111110; }
QToolButton:disabled { color: #b7b7ba; }

/* Labels never paint a background of their own. Without this a QLabel on a
   dark desktop theme draws the system window colour behind its text; the
   painted components (Pill, Avatar, ToolBadge, IconPad) set their own
   background via a widget stylesheet, which outranks this rule. */
QLabel {
    background: transparent;
}

QLabel:disabled {
    color: #b7b7ba;
}

/* ── groupbox (setup dialogs) ────────────────────────────────────────── */
QGroupBox {
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px solid #D8D7D2;
    border-radius: 12px;
    margin-top: 14px;
    padding-top: 14px;
    font-family: "Geist";
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 600;
}

QGroupBox::title {
    subcontrol-origin: margin;
    left: 11px;
    padding: 0 6px;
    color: #2a2a28;
}

/* ── scrollbars ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
QScrollArea {
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
}

QScrollArea > QWidget > QWidget {
    background: transparent;
}

QScrollBar:vertical {
    background: transparent;
    width: 9px;
    margin: 0;
}

QScrollBar::handle:vertical {
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.18);
    border-radius: 4px;
    min-height: 30px;
}

QScrollBar::handle:vertical:hover {
    background: #b7b7ba;
}

QScrollBar::add-line:vertical, QScrollBar::sub-line:vertical { height: 0; }
QScrollBar::add-page, QScrollBar::sub-page { background: transparent; }
QScrollBar:horizontal { height: 0; }

QSplitter::handle { background: #EFEEEA; }

/* ── chrome ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
QStatusBar {
    background: #111110;
    color: #EEEDEA;
    border-top: none;
    font-family: "Geist Mono";
    font-size: 11px;
}

QStatusBar::item { border: none; }

QMenu {
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid #D8D7D2;
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 4px;
    color: #111110;
}

QMenu::item {
    padding: 7px 20px 7px 12px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    color: #111110;
}

QMenu::item:selected {
    background: #EFEEEA;
    color: #111110;
}

QMenu::separator {
    height: 1px;
    background: #E6E5E1;
    margin: 4px 0;
}

/* ── the inquiry register ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * A work surface, not an orientation surface: rows are tight, dividers are
 * hairlines rather than zebra stripes, and the numeric columns are right
 * aligned so they can be scanned down. Every accent hex below is one of the
 * eleven the role swap already knows, so the register follows the member's
 * role like everything else.                                                 */
QTableView#registerTable {
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
    gridline-color: transparent;
    selection-background-color: #F6F5F2;
    selection-color: #111110;
}

QTableView#registerTable::item {
    padding: 0 10px;
    border: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #E6E5E1;
}

QTableView#registerTable::item:selected {
    background: #F6F5F2;
    color: #111110;
}

QTableView#registerTable QHeaderView::section:horizontal {
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #D8D7D2;
    padding: 0 10px 8px 10px;
    font-family: "Geist";
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.7px;
    color: #98989b;
}

QTableView#registerTable QHeaderView::section:horizontal:hover {
    color: #2a2a28;
}

/* ── Email inquiry automation: opaque operational work surface ────────────
   The dashboard wallpaper is useful for orientation, but an inquiry register
   contains names, dates, quantities and quotation state.  Those facts must
   stay readable over every wallpaper, not just a dark or low-contrast one. */
#inquiryWorkspace #toolbar {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.94);
    border: 1px solid #D8D7D2;
}

#inquiryWorkspace #inquiryTabBar {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.82);
    border: 1px solid #ffffff;
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 3px;
}

#inquiryWorkspace #inquiryTabBar::tab {
    color: #6b6a65;
    margin: 0;
}

#inquiryWorkspace #inquiryTabBar::tab:selected {
    background: #ffffff;
    color: #111110;
    border: 1px solid #D8D7D2;
}

#inquiryWorkspace QTabWidget::pane {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.86);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.80);
}

#inquiryWorkspace QTableWidget#inquiryTable {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.96);
    alternate-background-color: #f6f5f2;
    border: 1px solid #D8D7D2;
    gridline-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06);
    selection-background-color: #EFEEEA;
    selection-color: #111110;
    color: #2a2a28;
}

#inquiryWorkspace QTableWidget#inquiryTable::item {
    color: #2a2a28;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #E6E5E1;
}

#inquiryWorkspace QTableWidget#inquiryTable::item:selected {
    background: #EFEEEA;
    color: #111110;
}

#inquiryWorkspace QTableWidget#inquiryTable QHeaderView::section {
    background: #f6f5f2;
    border: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #D8D7D2;
    color: #6b6a65;
}

#inquiryWorkspace #meta {
    color: #6b6a65;
}

/* Mailbox checks are an ongoing background action, not a warning. The global
   bar uses a deliberately chunky purple treatment for media work; this thin,
   monochrome sweep is quieter and reads cleanly at the top of a register. */
#inquiryWorkspace QProgressBar#inquiryProgress {
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
    min-height: 22px;
    max-height: 22px;
    min-width: 50px;
    max-width: 50px;
    padding: 0;
}

#inquiryWorkspace QProgressBar#inquiryProgress::chunk {
    background: transparent;
    width: 0px;
    margin: 0;
}

/* ── sleek glassmorphic scrollbars ─────────────────────────────────────── */
QScrollBar:vertical {
    background: transparent;
    width: 6px;
    margin: 0px;
    border: none;
}

QScrollBar::handle:vertical {
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15);
    min-height: 24px;
    border-radius: 3px;
}

QScrollBar::handle:vertical:hover {
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.28);
}

QScrollBar::sub-line:vertical {
    height: 0px;
    width: 0px;
    subcontrol-position: top;
    subcontrol-origin: margin;
}

QScrollBar::add-line:vertical {
    height: 0px;
    width: 0px;
    subcontrol-position: bottom;
    subcontrol-origin: margin;
}

QScrollBar::up-arrow:vertical, QScrollBar::down-arrow:vertical {
    width: 0px;
    height: 0px;
    background: none;
}

QScrollBar::add-page:vertical, QScrollBar::sub-page:vertical {
    background: none;
}

QScrollBar:horizontal {
    background: transparent;
    height: 6px;
    margin: 0px;
    border: none;
}

QScrollBar::handle:horizontal {
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15);
    min-width: 24px;
    border-radius: 3px;
}

QScrollBar::handle:horizontal:hover {
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.28);
}

QScrollBar::sub-line:horizontal {
    width: 0px;
    height: 0px;
    subcontrol-position: left;
    subcontrol-origin: margin;
}

QScrollBar::add-line:horizontal {
    width: 0px;
    height: 0px;
    subcontrol-position: right;
    subcontrol-origin: margin;
}

QScrollBar::left-arrow:horizontal, QScrollBar::right-arrow:horizontal {
    width: 0px;
    height: 0px;
    background: none;
}

QScrollBar::add-page:horizontal, QScrollBar::sub-page:horizontal {
    background: none;
}

/* ── Dashboard (Home) Redesign Styles ────────────────────────────── */
#homeSearchPill {
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid #E6E5E1;
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 3px 12px;
}

#homeSearchPill:hover, #homeSearchPill:focus-within {
    background: #ffffff;
    border-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.18);
}

#homeSearchInput {
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
    font-size: 14px;
    color: #111110;
}

#homeKbdBadge {
    background: #EFEEEA;
    border: 1px solid #D8D7D2;
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #6b6a65;
}



#heroPromptCard {
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid #E6E5E1;
    border-radius: 18px;
}

#heroPromptInput {
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: #111110;
    padding: 4px 0px;
}

#promptChipBtn {
    background: #F6F5F2;
    border: 1px solid #E6E5E1;
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 5px 12px;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #2a2a28;
}

#promptChipBtn:hover {
    background: #EFEEEA;
    border-color: #D8D7D2;
}

#promptSendBtn {
    background: #111110;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 999px;
    min-width: 36px;
    max-width: 36px;
    min-height: 36px;
    max-height: 36px;
}

#promptSendBtn:hover {
    background: #2a2a28;
}

#tryChip {
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid #E6E5E1;
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 4px 12px;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: #2a2a28;
}

#tryChip:hover {
    background: #ffffff;
    border-color: #D8D7D2;
}

#tourCard {
    background-color: #0b1120;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.15);
    border-radius: 18px;
}

#tourPlayBtn {
    background: #ffffff;
    color: #111110;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 7px 16px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 14px;
}

#tourPlayBtn:hover {
    background: #f6f5f2;
}

#toolTile {
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid #E6E5E1;
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 6px;
}

#toolTile:hover {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.92);
    border-color: #D8D7D2;
}

#recentMenuBtn {
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 4px;
}

#recentMenuBtn:hover {
    background: #EFEEEA;
}
